       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day for adults. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit. At that dose, the risks include serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI bleeding, and hyponatremia. Higher doses also haven't been shown to work better.\n\nPlease tell me which of these you'd like:\n\n1. **Enter 200 mg PO once daily**, the maximum labeled dose. If the patient is starting treatment, the usual start is 25\u201350 mg daily, titrated up.\n2. **Enter a different dose or frequency.** Tell me what you intended. For example, 400 mg may have been a typo for 40 mg or 100 mg.\n3. **Enter 400 mg as written.** This is only if it's intentional, such as a specialist-directed regimen. Please confirm that, and I'll add a note to the order saying the dose is above the usual maximum and was confirmed by you.\n\nI'll enter whichever you choose."
